    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d176">

                <pb facs="0262" n="142" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg142"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Coolidge to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-05-04"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1876.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that on April 27
                    the Japanese minister handed me a pro memoria with regard to certain alleged
                    preparations of the Russian war vessels interned at Shanghai for active service.
                    He also stated that his government had made representations on the subject to
                    the American and British Governments. I immediately telegraphed to Mr. Davidson,
                    in Shanghai, for information, and on receipt of his reply wired to the
                    Department, as confirmed below.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Gardner
                    Coolidge.</hi></signed></closer>




